  "body": "## Repo Truth Extractor \u2014 deep audit + remediation\n\nFull audit of the RTE (`services/repo-truth-extractor/`) across prescan/scan, cost profiles, prompts, CLI/UX, ops and docs, plus the remediation that followed. Dry-run only throughout: **no live paid LLM call was made at any point**, and every cost figure is arithmetic against recorded rates, never a real invoice.\n\n### Provenance \u2014 rebuilt on current `main`\n\nThis head is a **fresh-base transplant**, not the previous branch. The prior head (`bf1842e3d0`) carried commit history unrelated to this programme, so it was rebuilt rather than merged or replayed.\n\n- Source head (bound): `bf1842e3d0b20396e6d222dccbe97257584849e2`\n- Rebuilt onto: `origin/main` `4c5856f32f`\n- Method: file-level transplant. The branch was **not merged**; its commits were **not replayed**. Only two files were touched by both sides since the merge-base.\n\n**Fidelity check.** Diffing the rebuilt tree against the source head yields differences only in (a) main's own `dope-context` advancement \u2014 28 files it added after the merge-base \u2014 and (b) the two deliberately reconciled files below. **Zero unexplained differences.** The resulting delta is byte-for-byte the same file set and the same 366 / +46,846 / \u22123,533 totals as the source PR.\n\n**Reconciled by hand** (the only overlapping files):\n- `pyproject.toml` \u2014 kept main's `voyageai>=0.5.0,<0.6` and `qdrant-client<2.0` bounds; added `pytest-timeout` and `ruff` to the `test` extra.\n- `uv.lock` \u2014 **regenerated** with `uv lock`, not merged. Resolves to main's lock plus exactly those two packages (+42, 0 deletions).\n\n### Deletion ledger \u2014 3,533 lines, 1 file\n\n`intentional-deletion` is required. Every deleted line is accounted for:\n\n| Area | Lines | What |\n|---|---|---|\n| `services/repo-truth-extractor/` | \u22123,074 | Monolith seam extraction \u2014 code **moved** out of `run_extraction_v5.py` (\u22121,993) into `extractor/{ui,cli_args,costing,phases}/`, and `lib/spend_ledger.py` (\u2212470) consolidated into the single pricing authority. Moves, not losses. |\n| `src/dopemux/` | \u2212314 | `extract_commands.truth_run`'s unreachable body (\u2212272; the function raises unconditionally as its first statement), plus two dead conditionals in the wizard preflight. |\n| `docs/` | \u2212133 | **The one deleted file**: `docs/04-explanation/root-relocated/user-journey.md`, a byte-identical duplicate of the archived copy (both `sha256 8d69906\u2026`), whose live-tree version documented `dopemux upgrades apply` \u2014 a command that has never existed. Archived copy kept as canonical; zero inbound links verified. |\n| other | \u221212 | `pytest.ini`, `ci-complete.yml`, root tests. |\n\n### The finding that mattered most\n\n**CI had executed zero jobs on this branch.** A backslash-escaped string literal in a GitHub Actions expression (`|| \\'missing\\'`) made the workflow file invalid, so all 14 required gates were **absent rather than failing** \u2014 while the PR's check list still read green. Repairing it exposed two more gates that had never worked once: `ruff` was declared nowhere in the repo (`extractor-lint` had never succeeded), and `pytest-timeout` was in `pyproject.toml` but never in `uv.lock`, so `uv sync --frozen` never installed it.\n\nAll four defects came from this programme's own earlier packets, each self-certified with a substring grep \u2014 a check that cannot distinguish *text present* from *workflow valid*. The recurrence guard is a **pre-commit** hook, deliberately not a CI job, since CI cannot catch what stops CI from starting.\n\n### What landed (12 packets)\n\n- **R0-006/007/009** \u2014 gate reports out of the worktree; F-07 dead code (one item was misfiled: a duplicated `compose.yml` target was re-ingesting that file into every phase-A corpus, since `Collector.collect()` does not de-duplicate \u2014 a wasted-spend defect, proven against the live collector); CI repair above.\n- **R2-002/004/005** \u2014 calibrated tokenizer with printed assumptions; go-live gate fails closed on un-opted skips, gpt-5 temperature rejection root-caused, webhook capability URL no longer emitted to stdout; walker/prescan repairs.\n- **R3-003/005a/006** \u2014 schema expansion; prompt content fixes (H9 no longer asks a model to compute a `sha256` the runtime already derives from real bytes); per-claim upstream attribution.\n- **R4-002/004/005/006** \u2014 `rte` is now the canonical CLI definition site with `upgrades` a hidden alias sharing the same objects (parity proven by enumeration); `rte status` no longer fabricates the run it reports on; docs steered to `rte`; unreachable `truth_run` body removed.\n\n### Verification\n\nService suite **1,686 \u2192 1,750 passed on CI, 0 xfailed**. Every fix was mutation-checked **by execution** \u2014 revert it, observe the real failure, restore \u2014 not asserted. Four tree-sitter-gated prescan deferrals are now proven to pass on a complete environment.\n\nTwo honest limits are recorded rather than glossed: the `promptsets/v4/schemas/*.schema.json` files are an **offline validation lane** that the request-time schema builder never loads, and no cost estimate was validated against live billing.\n\n### Not done\n\n`R4-004` Priority 2 (F-43/F-44 \u2014 notably the wizard's static pricing snapshot, which will drift from the authority established here), `R4-003`, `R5-001`, `R3-005b\u2013d`, the `D-*` deferrals, and `R0-008` (blocked on an operator decision about which committed extraction runs are load-bearing).\n\n### Merge requirements\n\n1. `intentional-deletion` label on **this** head (the ledger above is the justification).\n2. `independent embedded audit` passing, or an accepted signed local attestation present at this head.\n3. PR Steward evaluating this exact SHA.\n4. Squash-merge.\n",
