      "messageBody": "\u2026ant)\n\nRepo Truth Extractor deep audit and remediation. Rebuilt on current main as a\nfresh-base transplant per supervisor verdict BLOCKED_FRESH_BASE_CANDIDATE_REQUIRED;\nthe previous head carried commit history unrelated to this programme.\n\nPROVENANCE\n  source head (bound):  bf1842e3d0b20396e6d222dccbe97257584849e2\n  rebuilt onto:         origin/main 4c5856f32f\n  method: file-level transplant. The branch was NOT merged and its commits were\n  NOT replayed. Only two files were touched by both sides since the merge-base\n  (pyproject.toml, uv.lock); every other path was taken from the source head\n  verbatim. Fidelity was verified by diffing the rebuilt tree against the source\n  head: the only differences are main's own dope-context advancement (28 files)\n  plus the two reconciled files. Zero unexplained differences.\n\nRECONCILED BY HAND (the only overlapping files)\n  pyproject.toml \u2014 kept main's voyageai>=0.5.0,<0.6 and qdrant-client<2.0\n    bounds; added pytest-timeout and ruff to the `test` extra.\n  uv.lock \u2014 regenerated with `uv lock` rather than merged; resolves to main's\n    lock plus exactly the two added packages (+42 lines, 0 deletions).\n\nDELETION LEDGER \u2014 3533 lines, 1 file\n  services/repo-truth-extractor/  -3074   monolith seam extraction: code moved\n      out of run_extraction_v5.py (-1993) into extractor/{ui,cli_args,costing,\n      phases}/, and lib/spend_ledger.py (-470) consolidated into the single\n      pricing authority established by R2-001. Moves, not losses.\n  src/dopemux/                     -314   extract_commands.truth_run's\n      unreachable body (-272; the function raises unconditionally as its first\n      statement) plus two dead conditionals in the wizard preflight.\n  docs/                            -133   one deleted file,\n      docs/04-explanation/root-relocated/user-journey.md: a byte-identical\n      duplicate of the archived copy (both sha256 8d69906...), whose live-tree\n      version documented `dopemux upgrades apply`, a command that has never\n      existed. Archived copy retained as canonical; zero inbound links.\n  remaining -12 across pytest.ini, ci-complete.yml and root tests.\n\nSCOPE\n  services/repo-truth-extractor  257 files   task-packets  47\n  proof bundles                   20         claudedocs    11\n  docs                            13         src/dopemux    6\n  root/global                      6         root tests     3\n  scripts                          2         CI workflows   1\n\nWHAT LANDED (12 packets)\n  R0-009  CI had executed ZERO jobs on this branch: a backslash-escaped string\n          literal in a GitHub Actions expression made the workflow file invalid,\n          so all 14 required gates were ABSENT rather than failing while the PR\n          read green. Also repaired a dangling shell continuation that would\n          have kept extractor-full permanently red, installed ruff (declared\n          nowhere in the repo, so extractor-lint had never once succeeded), and\n          got pytest-timeout into uv.lock (added to pyproject but never locked,\n          so `uv sync --frozen` never installed it). Added a pre-commit guard \u2014\n          deliberately NOT a CI job, since CI cannot catch what stops CI\n          starting.\n  R0-006  pre-live gate no longer writes reports into the repo worktree.\n  R0-007  F-07 dead code. One item was misfiled: a duplicated \"compose.yml\"\n          target was re-ingesting that file into every phase-A corpus, because\n          Collector.collect() does not de-duplicate \u2014 proven against the live\n          collector. A wasted-spend defect, not cosmetics.\n  R2-002  calibrated tokenizer, per-lane output ratios, printed assumptions.\n  R2-004  go-live gate fails closed on un-opted-in skips; gpt-5 temperature\n          rejection root-caused; webhook capability URL no longer emitted.\n  R2-005  walker/prescan repairs; 3 WALKER-006 deferrals closed, 3 relabelled.\n  R3-003  schema expansion, with the honest disclosure that these .schema.json\n          files are an offline lane the request-time builder never loads.\n  R3-005a prompt content fixes; H9 no longer asks a model to compute a sha256\n          the runtime already computes from real bytes.\n  R3-006  per-claim upstream attribution, proven to bind at request time.\n  R4-002  `rte` is now the canonical CLI definition site; `upgrades` a hidden\n          alias sharing the same objects, with enumerated parity.\n  R4-004  F-59: `rte status` fabricated the run it reported on \u2014 it minted a new\n          run id, materialised its directory, then reported that empty run while\n          the operator's real run was never shown. Priority 2 (F-43/F-44) is\n          explicitly NOT done.\n  R4-005  docs steered to the canonical `rte` surface.\n  R4-006  unreachable truth_run body removed; generated-promptset recorded as\n          disposable (a regenerate-and-diff gate is unworkable while\n          _compute_repo_hash hashes the absolute repo path).\n\nVERIFICATION\n  Service suite 1686 -> 1750 passed on CI, 0 xfailed. Every fix was\n  mutation-checked by execution \u2014 revert, observe real failure, restore \u2014 not\n  asserted. Four tree-sitter-gated prescan deferrals are proven to pass on a\n  complete environment.\n\nNOT DONE, recorded rather than implied closed: R4-004 Priority 2, R4-003,\nR5-001, R3-005b-d, the D-* deferrals, and R0-008 (blocked on an operator\ndecision about which committed extraction runs are load-bearing).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
